markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Misconceptions to Watch For

Teachers new to this unit often bring a few beliefs that can work against it. Each one below comes from the unit's lesson plans and teacher notes.

## "I need a strong math or computer science background."

The unit uses tables, yes/no questions, and percentages. Every concept starts with an unplugged activity before students open AI Studio.

## "Vocabulary should be memorized first."

Terms come after the experience and help students explain precisely. Drilling definitions pulls attention away from the reasoning the unit builds.

## "Wrong guesses should be corrected right away."

Early predictions are hypotheses the lesson tests. The teacher notes ask you to hold off on confirming answers so students find the reason themselves.

## "A higher accuracy score means a better model."

Accuracy only measures whether a model matches its labels, often on a small test set. A model can score well and still fail some people.

## "The unplugged activities are optional warm-ups."

Card sorts and the Human Decision Tree build the ideas that the AI Studio work depends on. Skipping them makes the later lessons harder.
MARKDOWN
